WEBVTT

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:10.430
I'll show you the power of Abigail.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:04.060
It's over.

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:08.540
Abigail is back, sealed away no longer.

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:11.230
The world is ending.

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:47.140
What happened?

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:48.720
What is that light?

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.280
It's so pretty.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:52.530
Dante...

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:57.970
Lady! What are you doing here?

00:01:57.970 --> 00:02:00.200
Looks like it's finally started.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.910
What's started?

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:11.540
Alan Lowell?

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:15.310
There was once an alchemist by that name.

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:20.260
He was a human, but he was also a
sorcerer who employed various devils.

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:22.850
That was Alan Lowell?

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:23.340
Right.

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:25.760
Lowell...

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:30.950
There was just one devil that Alan
couldn't bend to his employment.

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:36.240
And that was Abigail, who was said to
have powers on par with the demon king's.

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:45.160
Using every bit of power he possessed,
Alan successfully sealed away Abigail's powers.

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:51.600
But seal them away was all he did.
He was unable to accomplish any more.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:57.810
So to prevent Abigail's powers
from falling into anyone's hands,

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:00.180
Alan constructed many magical
barriers and spread them around.

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:04.350
Barriers so tight even a single
ant couldn't pass through.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:09.050
Something came into being during the process
of making those barriers: the magic stone,

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:11.560
"Alan's Tear."

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:17.420
You know more about that than
anyone else, right, Nina Lowell?

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:25.780
I protected that magic stone according
to the ages-old tradition of our family.

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:29.750
That pendant, which could become
the key to unlock the seal on Abigail...

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:33.450
And all I could do was keep on running.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:36.480
Why didn't you try to do
anything about the pendant

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:39.460
before you spent ten years on the run?

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:44.800
What was I supposed to do? Throw
away a pendant that summoned demons?

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:49.530
And yet, even if you destroyed the
stone, it would just break the seal.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:53.070
Either way, it's all over.

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:56.300
The seal has been broken.

00:03:56.300 --> 00:04:01.120
With Abigail's powers on his side,
no one could stop that devil anymore.

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:04.840
Because Alan Lowell is
no longer in this world.

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:06.600
Then what about Dante?

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:09.930
It's impossible. No matter
how strong he may be,

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:13.080
there's no way he could defy Abigail's power.

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:19.860
Watch out!

00:04:28.730 --> 00:04:30.690
Hurry up and get away from here.

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:33.970
Shouldn't you get it in
gear and run away, too?

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:35.350
There's no point.

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:41.190
He won't be stopped now. No one can stop him!

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:44.690
Looks like he's shown himself.

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:49.320
What is that thing?!

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:56.420
Abigail.

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:20.990
The end of the world, eh?

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:32.220
Hey, hold it there, Patty!
Where do you think you're going?

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:35.260
Let me go! Let me go, Lady!

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:36.660
What do you mean to do?

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:39.690
Isn't it obvious? I'm
going to go fetch Dante!

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:41.360
That's crazy. You'll get yourself killed!

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:42.640
I don't care if I do!

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:46.620
--Patty!
--Wait.

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:48.350
I'll go too!

00:05:48.350 --> 00:05:49.510
You...

00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:54.090
Honestly! All he does is give me trouble.

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:56.160
I'll leave the rest to you!

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:58.040
Hey, what do you mean by that?!

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:01.160
It's worth placing a bet on.

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:04.230
The two descendants of Alan Lowell...

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:07.610
A miracle might happen.

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:10.070
Are you really the type
to believe in miracles?

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:14.170
Yeah...

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:19.630
Just this once, I'm starting to
want to believe in miracles, too.

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:53.400
Patty! Don't go charging on ahead of us!

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:59.560
It's no good, we can't get through this.

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:03.440
But if we don't get through here, we
can't get to the south wing's top floor...

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:06.710
All right, there has to be a
sprinkler control valve somewhere.

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:09.050
You wait here.

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:18.060
I'm sorry.

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:25.350
I didn't think something
this bad would happen; I...

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:27.700
Mom?

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:31.310
No, I'm sorry.

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:34.100
I'm sorry...

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:37.050
Patty!

00:07:39.870 --> 00:07:45.240
For making you lonely...
for such a long time...

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:51.620
Mom...

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:02.890
Well, this beats me. A little
cooler in here now, huh, you t...

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:38.850
How many of these small
fries do we have to fight?

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:40.470
My, are you tired already?

00:08:40.470 --> 00:08:41.780
As if.

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:51.230
How nice for you. It looks
like this fry isn't quite so small.

00:08:53.190 --> 00:08:55.970
Well, not small in body anyway.

00:09:02.840 --> 00:09:07.260
Sheesh, when I think about how I'm
not gonna get paid for this, I could cry!

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:11.800
Why not send Dante a bill afterwards?

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:13.780
Sure, if he's alive.

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:23.620
Awfully quiet, isn't it?

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:27.390
So, what are we supposed to do?

00:09:27.390 --> 00:09:29.350
I don't know either.

00:09:29.350 --> 00:09:32.230
What do you mean you don't know?

00:09:32.230 --> 00:09:33.900
Isn't there a rite or a spell or something?

00:09:38.560 --> 00:09:39.720
Dante...

00:09:42.110 --> 00:09:42.960
Patty!

00:09:49.050 --> 00:09:49.980
Patty!

00:10:10.770 --> 00:10:11.940
Dante!

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:16.360
Dante!

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:26.730
What was with those devils?

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:37.550
Patty... That pendant...

00:10:44.110 --> 00:10:46.090
--Patty!
--Hey, wait, Patty!

00:10:50.230 --> 00:10:52.560
What's happening? Where did Patty go?

00:10:52.990 --> 00:10:54.700
The demon realm, I would think.

00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:55.830
The demon realm?

00:10:55.830 --> 00:10:59.980
But the pendant Patty has
contains a shard of Alan's Tear.

00:10:59.980 --> 00:11:02.370
It doesn't have as much power as Alan's Tear,

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:04.880
but it's got enough
magic to at least protect her.

00:11:34.110 --> 00:11:35.200
Dante...

00:11:42.310 --> 00:11:44.650
Where are you, Dante?

00:11:56.410 --> 00:11:57.680
This way?

00:12:04.090 --> 00:12:06.900
Hey, there's just no end to these things!

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:11.600
Agreed. And it looks like
he's creating these minions, so...

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:15.390
So basically, if we don't rub
him out, this'll just keep going?

00:12:15.390 --> 00:12:16.420
Probably.

00:12:19.160 --> 00:12:21.890
Say, would you lend me a hand?

00:13:04.910 --> 00:13:06.630
Pretty pathetic, huh?

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:10.490
So we've really just got
to rely on him, is that it?

00:13:24.860 --> 00:13:26.160
Dante!

00:13:26.810 --> 00:13:28.730
Dante! Dante!

00:13:34.430 --> 00:13:35.400
Dante...

00:13:55.990 --> 00:13:56.980
Dante!

00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:01.250
Dante! Dante!

00:14:01.250 --> 00:14:04.260
Dante, wake up! Run away!

00:14:04.260 --> 00:14:06.020
Dante!

00:14:06.980 --> 00:14:08.980
I'll take that out for you right now.

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:21.690
There's no way you'd die of a
little wound like this, right Dante?

00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:27.740
Please, wake up! And then take
down the devil like you always do!

00:14:30.280 --> 00:14:32.660
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:35.050
It's my fault, isn't it?

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:38.760
I'm sorry, Dante. Are you mad?

00:14:39.220 --> 00:14:42.670
But I don't want this! I can't
stand to have this be our goodbye!

00:14:43.640 --> 00:14:46.970
I... I haven't even said thank you yet!

00:14:47.450 --> 00:14:50.600
It was so much fun getting
to be with you, but I haven't...

00:14:50.600 --> 00:14:51.550
Dante!

00:14:52.550 --> 00:14:54.720
Dante, please, open your eyes!

00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:57.850
I won't get mad at you for
messing up your office anymore!

00:14:57.850 --> 00:15:00.730
And I won't eat your strawberry
sundaes without asking, either!

00:15:00.730 --> 00:15:02.080
Please!

00:15:07.650 --> 00:15:11.220
Dante!

00:15:29.720 --> 00:15:30.830
Dante...

00:15:43.640 --> 00:15:47.580
There's no need to be afraid, little lady.

00:15:50.150 --> 00:15:53.310
I just want to say a little "thank you."

00:15:54.250 --> 00:16:02.230
After all, thanks to you, I was able
to get enough power to rule the world.

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:09.360
Hmph, you're no match for Dante.
When he comes he'll take you down for sure!

00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:16.720
Dante's dead, girl.

00:16:16.720 --> 00:16:19.370
There's no way Dante would
die at the hands of someone like--

00:16:20.730 --> 00:16:22.760
Mom... Morrison...

00:16:26.310 --> 00:16:28.190
Run, Patty...

00:16:34.600 --> 00:16:37.060
Dante!

00:16:42.440 --> 00:16:43.470
What?!

00:17:16.420 --> 00:17:19.340
Is it... Is it really you, Dante?

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:23.320
Is there another man this
attractive out there?

00:17:26.220 --> 00:17:28.200
Dante, that's...

00:17:29.540 --> 00:17:31.250
Oh, this?

00:17:31.770 --> 00:17:34.680
It looks like a certain
someone played a trick on me

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:37.650
while I was having myself a nice little nap.

00:17:43.030 --> 00:17:44.090
Perfect timing.

00:17:44.900 --> 00:17:47.020
The rest of the show is adults-only.

00:17:53.260 --> 00:17:57.950
Patty, this is one time I
might owe you a "thank you."

00:17:58.640 --> 00:17:59.960
You wait there.

00:17:59.960 --> 00:18:03.150
As a reward, I'll give him a good
lashing from you after I deliver mine.

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:08.630
Anybody who pulls pranks like
this needs to be taught a lesson.

00:18:09.410 --> 00:18:11.840
Morrison, I'll leave the rest to you.

00:18:11.840 --> 00:18:15.250
Damn, you make me wait forever, and
then you go making selfish requests...

00:18:16.330 --> 00:18:17.260
Sorry.

00:18:23.640 --> 00:18:25.470
It looks like it's finally going to begin.

00:18:25.470 --> 00:18:28.600
Jeez, Dante sure took his sweet time!

00:18:29.910 --> 00:18:34.230
Heh, you've grown since I last saw you.

00:18:34.230 --> 00:18:36.940
I'll pay you back for what
you did, make no mistake.

00:18:36.940 --> 00:18:39.470
Can you?

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:41.850
After all, right now I have enough power

00:18:41.850 --> 00:18:46.780
to rule even the human world,
let alone the demon one.

00:18:46.780 --> 00:18:50.290
I've had just about enough
of your arrogant attitude.

00:19:11.690 --> 00:19:15.570
In the end, child's play like
this is the most you can do.

00:19:26.130 --> 00:19:28.630
Th-This can't be!

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:32.080
You can grow as big as you want,

00:19:32.670 --> 00:19:36.880
and you can get yourself
world-dominating power...

00:19:40.690 --> 00:19:42.090
...but it's pointless!

00:20:04.550 --> 00:20:05.780
Hey, now!

00:20:10.550 --> 00:20:14.810
Wh-Why? Why can't I win?!

00:20:14.810 --> 00:20:18.750
I got power that was
top-class in the demon world!

00:20:18.750 --> 00:20:23.850
I don't care how strong you are,
something is wrong with this picture!

00:20:23.850 --> 00:20:28.170
Dammit, this is totally unfair!

00:20:28.770 --> 00:20:31.390
Is it decided from the
moment we're born, then?!

00:20:31.390 --> 00:20:37.970
That demons born without much power
are fated to be stamped out by you?!

00:20:37.970 --> 00:20:40.540
I can't believe that!

00:20:40.540 --> 00:20:43.890
If this is how things are, no
matter what I do, it's meaningless...

00:20:43.890 --> 00:20:46.220
That's not it. It's about souls.

00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:47.240
Huh?

00:20:47.240 --> 00:20:50.690
Basically, someone like
you who's let his soul rot

00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:56.400
can't measure up to someone with a
real soul just by getting some power.

00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:05.270
Well then, strong, gentle
Lord Dante of the "real soul,"

00:21:05.270 --> 00:21:09.510
you'll let me live even now, won't you?

00:21:09.510 --> 00:21:11.760
Just like you have before.

00:21:11.760 --> 00:21:15.430
No can do. You went too far.

00:21:15.950 --> 00:21:19.440
But you know, I kinda liked you.

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:24.240
Y-You bastard!

00:21:25.390 --> 00:21:26.850
Jackpot.

00:21:39.200 --> 00:21:41.330
Dante!

00:21:42.150 --> 00:21:46.590
Hey, now, go easy on me.
I'm injured, you know.

00:21:46.590 --> 00:21:48.620
S-Sorry.

00:21:49.600 --> 00:21:50.940
--Patty.
--Huh?

00:21:51.690 --> 00:21:56.060
You'll always be with your mother
from now on. Have a happy life.

00:22:03.400 --> 00:22:08.440
Hey, Morrison, drive me to the office.
Your car will still move, right?

00:22:08.440 --> 00:22:13.220
You're such a slave-driver.
I'm injured too, here!

00:22:46.360 --> 00:22:48.490
I see someone's in a bad mood.

00:22:49.010 --> 00:22:52.350
Patty's departure really
did a number on you, huh?

00:22:52.350 --> 00:22:53.560
What do you want?

00:22:53.560 --> 00:22:55.840
Don't be stupid.

00:22:56.190 --> 00:23:00.910
There's only one reason I'd come
all the way over to your office, right?

00:23:00.910 --> 00:23:03.940
Then hurry up and tell me the deal.

00:23:03.940 --> 00:23:06.180
No small talk, thanks.

00:23:06.180 --> 00:23:09.910
Apparently a large number of devils
have showed up in a certain country.

00:23:09.910 --> 00:23:15.180
It's a sweet job. The client's
filthy rich, so the pay will be good.

00:23:20.700 --> 00:23:24.580
I hear little Patty's
doing well with her mom.

00:23:31.190 --> 00:23:33.930
Sorry, but I'm on my way to a job.

00:23:34.320 --> 00:23:36.560
I don't have time to hang out with you.

00:23:36.560 --> 00:23:37.960
My, what a coincidence.

00:23:38.450 --> 00:23:40.920
We're on our way to a job, too.

00:23:41.480 --> 00:23:43.630
I imagine we're all going to the same place.

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:45.830
So in other words...

00:23:46.290 --> 00:23:48.050
The pay for this job...

00:23:48.440 --> 00:23:50.770
...goes to the fastest one, of course!

00:23:51.190 --> 00:23:53.880
Fine, bring it on! Floor it, Morrison.

00:24:01.980 --> 00:24:03.210
I knew it.

00:24:04.140 --> 00:24:08.160
Really, that Dante trashes the
place right away if I'm not around!